      "author_association": "NONE",
      "body": "While attempting to use `ansible.builtin.deb822_repository` and including parameters to download the signed_by key from a remote URL in an environment that requires a proxy, I saw that it was not using the proxy and failing the download.  Curl works.\n\nThe proxy is configured using the standard `http(s)_proxy=...` environment variables.\n\nLooking at the code here:\nhttps://github.com/ansible/ansible/blob/54ccad9e460cb6bfa0ff585a46289239966b56cc/lib/ansible/module_utils/urls.py#L851\n\nIt appears that the intention of `use_proxy` is inverted.  Should it be:\n\n```diff \n-        if not use_proxy:\n+        if use_proxy:\n             proxyhandler = urllib.request.ProxyHandler({})\n             handlers.append(proxyhandler)\n```\n\n    ",
